            <note> (1830) without the fronispiece and the extra engraved title and with different plates for backgammon, draughts, and chess. Even the title page is the same setting of type except for the imprint (note the period rather than comma after Billiards in the list of games), suggesting that the book was produced from stereoplates. </note>
